From 7e96e371ab9af6e1545973e4630f881cb50d5e9c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ReArc Overlay <overlay@rearc.invalid>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 23:25:15 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] P-TAB-001 extension side panels: chrome.sidePanel as hosted
 panels for the host

Claude's and ChatGPT's extensions open a side panel next to the page
(sidePanel.setPanelBehavior({openPanelOnActionClick}), sidePanel.open).
Chrome shows it in its Views side panel, which needs a Browser window;
registry tabs and logical shell windows have none, so 1.33 only reported
run result 2 and sidePanel.open failed with "Tab not found". ABI 1.47
(extension_side_panels, bridge 0.49.0) gives the host the panel.

Options stay Chromium's SidePanelService (manifest default_path, setOptions
global or per tab, setPanelBehavior). ReArcTabGetSidePanel reports whether
an extension has a panel for a tab, whether it is the tab's own
(contextual) and whether a toolbar click opens it. ReArcTabOpenSidePanel
creates the panel like an action popup: a registry tab (disposition 3,
opener the page tab) with view type kExtensionSidePanel loading the
resolved panel URL (http(s) or extension path, as
ExtensionSidePanelCoordinator), in the original profile for spanning
extensions, with no history helper. ReArcSidePanelSetShown dispatches
sidePanel.onOpened / onClosed with the owner's logical window and, for
contextual panels, the tab. In the embedded engine sidePanel.open and
sidePanel.close become host events (ReArcEngineSetSidePanelCallback: kind 0
open, 1 close, 2 options changed) with Chromium's validation and error
strings; windowId resolves logical windows, WINDOW_ID_CURRENT the focused
one. Options changes navigate shown panels whose path changed and report
disabled ones. framework.exports and framework.order list the four new
functions. Existing ABI layouts remain unchanged.

Last rebased: 2026-11-06 onto Chromium 156.0.8078.74 (d331de35ca).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
